{# ============================================================================
   PEBBLE HEADER — one row, and a bar that changes shape on scroll
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ┌ announcement ─── message · language ───────────────── (optional, off) ┐
     │                                                                        │
     │   ┌ 24px ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
     │   │ Shop ⌄  Collections ⌄  …    LOGO    prompt  ⌕  ♡  🛒        │    │  scrollY = 0
     │   └──── white card · max 1200px · radius 8px ────────────────────┘    │
     │                                                                        │
     ├────────── the same row, edge to edge, radius 0 ──────────────────────┤  scrollY > 0
     └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   ── The shape change is the whole idea ──
   At the top of the page the bar is a CARD floating over the hero; the moment
   the page moves it spreads to the viewport edge. Measured off the reference:
   the height does NOT change (72px in both states) and the logo does NOT move
   (dead centre in both). Only three things animate — the bar's inline margin,
   its radius, and its top gap. Everything else is still.

   That is why the row is a `1fr auto 1fr` grid rather than a flex row: the
   centre column is centred on the BAR regardless of how wide the nav or the
   action cluster get, so the logo cannot drift by a few pixels as the bar
   resizes. A flex row with `justify-content: space-between` would have moved it.

   ── What the reference design has that Qumra does NOT, and what replaces it ──
   · A person icon           →  themes ship without one, and Qumra has no route
     for it here, so that icon would link to a 404.
     The slot is a merchant-defined link instead — `action_link_url` with a
     choice of icon — and it renders NOTHING until the merchant fills it in.
   · "Pages" / "Features" menus → those are demo-theme routes. The nav is
     `nav_item` blocks pointing at the pages Qumra actually serves; the field
     label lists them.
   · Mega menu with nested columns → the `menu` setting returns a FLAT list of
     `{ title, url }`; Qumra has no nested link lists. A nav item's dropdown is
     therefore that flat list split across 1–4 columns, with one optional promo
     image per item.

   ── The search field is a real form, not a decoration ──
   `/shop` IS the search results page: collectionFilter() in assets/main.js
   reads `?q=` from the URL on init, and reads the collection from the PATH
   (`/shop/<handle>`). The live dropdown calls Qumra.search.search(), which hits
   /ajax/search/products.

   Contracts with assets/main.js — do not rename:
     toggleModal('sidebar' | 'cart')  ·  $store.cart.totalQuantity
     Qumra.search.search
   All styling lives in assets/style.css → "15.1 HEADER".
   ========================================================================= #}

{# ---- External-link test ----
   Identical to the macro in widgets/footer/widget.njk, and duplicated rather
   than shared on purpose: ui/sidebar.njk is itself a `ui` partial included by
   this widget, and `{% ui %}` calling `{% ui %}` is a construct this theme
   bans outright (see the header of ui/cart.njk). Six characters of duplication
   beat reintroducing nested includes.

   `indexOf` rather than the `in` operator — `in` is written for arrays and
   dicts here and throws on an undefined string. The second test lets an
   absolute link to THIS store stay in-tab; `store.url` is guarded so a render
   without it cannot make every link external by accident. #}
{% macro extAttrs(url) %}{% if url and url.indexOf('://') > -1 and not (store.url and url.indexOf(store.url) == 0) %} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"{% endif %}{% endmacro %}

{% set id = widget.id %}
{% set d = widget.data %}
{% set navItems = widget.blocks | default([], true) %}

{% set storeName = store.name | default('', true) %}
{% set logo = d.header_logo if d.header_logo and d.header_logo.fileUrl else store.logo %}
{% set logoH = d.logo_height | default(30) %}

{# ---- Shape ----
   `floating` OFF means the bar is edge-to-edge from the first frame and never
   changes — which is also what `sticky` OFF has to imply, since a bar that
   scrolls away with the page has no "scrolled" state to spread into. Resolving
   that here rather than in the CSS keeps the two settings from contradicting
   each other in a way the merchant can see but not fix. #}
{% set isSticky = d.sticky | default(true) %}
{% set isFloat = (d.floating | default(true)) and isSticky %}
{% set floatW = d.float_width | default(1200) %}
{% set floatGap = d.float_gap | default(24) %}
{% set floatR = d.float_radius | default(8) %}

{% set showTop = d.topbar_enabled | default(false) %}
{% set topMsg = d.topbar_message | default('', true) %}
{% set topMsgUrl = d.topbar_message_url | default('', true) %}
{% set showLocale = d.topbar_show_locale | default(true) %}

{% set showSearch = d.show_search | default(true) %}
{% set searchStyle = d.search_style | default('inline', true) %}

{% set actionUrl = d.action_link_url | default('', true) %}
{# No person icon: themes ship without one, and a
   silhouette in the header reads as one whatever the link points to. A value
   saved before the option was removed falls back to the heart. #}
{% set actionIcon = d.action_link_icon | default('heart', true) %}
{% if actionIcon == 'user' %}{% set actionIcon = 'heart' %}{% endif %}
{% set showCart = d.show_cart | default(true) %}

{% set navOn = d.nav_enabled | default(true) %}
{% set navExtra = d.nav_extra_menu or false %}

{% set rawLang = localization.language | default('ar', true) %}
{% set currentLang = rawLang if rawLang == 'en' else 'ar' %}
{% set currencyCode = localization.currency.currencyCode | default('', true) %}

{# ---- Current path, for the active-link underline ----
   Trailing slashes are stripped so '/shop' and '/shop/' resolve to the same
   link. Home collapses to '' rather than '/', which is what lets the match be
   an equality test: with '/' kept, a startswith test would light up Home on
   every page and an equality test would fail on '/shop/'.

   `curFull` keeps the query. A nav item whose own URL carries one — the offers
   link is `/shop?sort=discount` — is a DIFFERENT destination from plain /shop,
   and comparing paths alone lit both of them at once. Items with a query
   therefore match on the whole URL, and if Qalab ever hands back a `page.url`
   with the query stripped they simply never match: a missing underline, never
   a wrong one. #}
{% set curFull = page.url | default('/', true) %}
{% set curPath = curFull.split('?')[0] %}
{% set curPath = curPath.slice(0, -1) if (curPath | length) > 1 and curPath.slice(-1) == '/' else curPath %}
{% set curPath = '' if curPath == '/' else curPath %}


{# ============================ MACROS ============================ #}

{# A menu picker hands back either { items: [...] } or a bare [...]. Normalise
   once here so every call site can just iterate. #}
{#- A menu item with `children` (the third level of a Qumra menu) becomes a
    small group: the item as its heading, the children under it. They used
    to be dropped, so a nested menu lost everything below the second level. -#}
{% macro menuLinks(menu, cls) %}
  {% for item in (menu.items if menu.items else menu) %}
    {% if item.children and (item.children | length) > 0 %}
      <div class="hy-drop-group">
        <a href="{{ item.url | default('#', true) }}"{{ extAttrs(item.url) }} class="{{ cls }} hy-drop-link--parent">{{ item.title }}</a>
        {% for ch in item.children %}
          <a href="{{ ch.url | default('#', true) }}"{{ extAttrs(ch.url) }} class="{{ cls }} hy-drop-sublink">{{ ch.title }}</a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% else %}
      <a href="{{ item.url | default('#', true) }}"{{ extAttrs(item.url) }} class="{{ cls }}">{{ item.title }}</a>
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
{% endmacro %}

{% macro caret(cls) %}
  <svg class="{{ cls | default('hy-caret', true) }}" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 12 12"
       fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" aria-hidden="true">
    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.5 4.5 6 8l3.5-3.5"/>
  </svg>
{% endmacro %}

{# The action-slot icon. Five shapes, one of which the merchant picks — a
   `select` rather than five booleans, because exactly one can be shown. #}
{% macro actionSvg(key) %}
  <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
       stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
    {% if key == 'heart' %}
      <path d="M12 20.3 4.8 13.4a4.4 4.4 0 0 1 6.2-6.2l1 1 1-1a4.4 4.4 0 0 1 6.2 6.2L12 20.3Z"/>
    {% elif key == 'whatsapp' %}
      <path d="M3.5 20.5 5 16.8A7.8 7.8 0 1 1 8 19.4l-4.5 1.1Z"/>
      <path d="M9 9.4c0 3 2.6 5.6 5.6 5.6"/>
    {% elif key == 'phone' %}
      <path d="M5 3.8h3.1l1.6 4-2 1.3a11.4 11.4 0 0 0 5.2 5.2l1.3-2 4 1.6v3.1a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-2 1.8A15.9 15.9 0 0 1 3.2 5.8a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8-2Z"/>
    {% elif key == 'truck' %}
      <path d="M2.8 7.2h9.4v9H2.8zM12.2 10.2h3.6l2.4 2.6v3.4h-6z"/>
      <circle cx="6.4" cy="18" r="1.7"/><circle cx="16.2" cy="18" r="1.7"/>
    {% else %}
      <circle cx="12" cy="8.2" r="3.6"/>
      <path d="M5.6 19.6a6.8 6.8 0 0 1 12.8 0"/>
    {% endif %}
  </svg>
{% endmacro %}


<header id="hy-header-{{ id }}"
        class="hy-header {{ 'is-sticky' if isSticky }} {{ 'has-float' if isFloat }} {{ 'is-float' if isFloat }}">

  {# ═══════════════════════ 1 · ANNOUNCEMENT ═══════════════════════
     Off by default — the reference preset has no strip, and an empty coloured
     band above a floating card reads as a mistake rather than as a choice. It
     stays available because "شحن مجاني فوق ٥٠٠" is the single most useful line
     a baby shop can put on every page. #}
  {% if showTop and (topMsg or showLocale) %}
    <div class="hy-topbar" id="hy-topbar-{{ id }}">
      {# Absolutely positioned rather than a fourth grid child: the row is a
         three-column grid (spacer · message · end) and a fourth cell would
         knock the message off centre. #}
      <button type="button"
              id="hy-topbarX-{{ id }}"
              class="hy-topbar-close"
              aria-label="{{ t('common.close') }}">
        <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
             stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M6 18 18 6M6 6l12 12"/>
        </svg>
      </button>

      <div class="hy-topbar-row">
        <span class="hy-topbar-start" aria-hidden="true"></span>

        {% if topMsg %}
          {% if topMsgUrl %}
            <a href="{{ topMsgUrl }}" class="hy-topbar-msg">{{ topMsg }}</a>
          {% else %}
            <p class="hy-topbar-msg">{{ topMsg }}</p>
          {% endif %}
        {% else %}
          <span class="hy-topbar-msg" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="hy-topbar-end">
          {% if showLocale %}
            {# The reference puts a country + currency picker here. Currency is
               resolved server-side from `localization.market` and there is
               nothing a shopper can post to, so it renders as a LABEL; the
               control beside it is the language switcher, which is real. #}
            <div class="hy-locale" x-data="{ open: false }" @click.outside="open = false">
              <button type="button"
                      class="hy-locale-btn"
                      @click="open = !open"
                      :aria-expanded="open ? 'true' : 'false'"
                      aria-label="{{ t('common.language') }}">
                <span>{{ 'English' if currentLang == 'en' else 'العربية' }}</span>
                {% if currencyCode %}<span class="hy-locale-cur">({{ currencyCode }})</span>{% endif %}
                {{ caret('hy-caret hy-caret--sm') }}
              </button>

              <div class="hy-locale-drop"
                   x-show="open" x-cloak
                   x-transition:enter="transition ease-out duration-200"
                   x-transition:enter-start="opacity-0 -translate-y-1"
                   x-transition:enter-end="opacity-100 translate-y-0"
                   x-transition:leave="transition ease-in duration-150"
                   x-transition:leave-start="opacity-100"
                   x-transition:leave-end="opacity-0">
                {% form 'lang' %}
                  <button type="submit" name="lang" value="ar" {% if currentLang == 'ar' %}disabled{% endif %}>
                    <span class="font-body">العربية</span>
                    {% if currentLang == 'ar' %}
                      <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 12.5 9.5 18 20 6.5"/></svg>
                    {% endif %}
                  </button>
                  <button type="submit" name="lang" value="en" {% if currentLang == 'en' %}disabled{% endif %}>
                    <span class="font-body-en">English</span>
                    {% if currentLang == 'en' %}
                      <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 12.5 9.5 18 20 6.5"/></svg>
                    {% endif %}
                  </button>
                {% endform %}
              </div>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {% endif %}


  {# ═══════════════════════ 2 · THE BAR ═══════════════════════
     One element carries the whole shape change. `.hy-hbar` is what gets the
     white ground, the radius and the margins; `.hy-hrow` inside it is the
     three-column grid that never moves. #}
  <div class="hy-hbar">
    <div class="hy-hrow"
         x-data="{
           open: null,
           _t: null,
           show(k) { clearTimeout(this._t); this.open = k },
           hide()  { clearTimeout(this._t); this._t = setTimeout(() => { this.open = null }, 160) },
           close() { clearTimeout(this._t); this.open = null }
         }"
         @keydown.escape.window="close()">

      {# ---- start: nav on desktop, burger on mobile ---- #}
      <div class="hy-hstart">
        <button type="button"
                onclick="toggleModal('sidebar')"
                class="hy-icon-btn hy-mob"
                aria-label="{{ t('common.menu') }}">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M3 7h18M3 12h18M3 17h18"/>
          </svg>
        </button>

        {% if navOn and ((navItems | length) > 0 or navExtra) %}
          <nav class="hy-nav hy-desk" aria-label="{{ t('common.menu') }}">
            {% for block in navItems %}
              {# Blocks arrive wrapped — the settings live on `.data`, never on
                 the block itself. Reading b.nav_label off the wrapper yields
                 undefined, the guard below goes false, and the whole nav
                 renders as nothing with no error anywhere. #}
              {% set b = block.data %}
              {% if b.nav_label %}
                {% set links = b.nav_menu.items if b.nav_menu and b.nav_menu.items else b.nav_menu %}
                {% set hasDrop = links and (links | length) > 0 %}
                {% set cols = b.nav_columns | default('1', true) %}
                {% set promo = b.nav_image.fileUrl if b.nav_image and b.nav_image.fileUrl else '' %}
                {% set wide = cols != '1' %}

                {# Normalise the block's own URL the same way the current path
                   was, so '/shop/' and '/shop' compare equal. #}
                {% set bRaw = b.nav_url | default('', true) %}
                {% set bUrl = bRaw.split('?')[0] %}
                {% set bUrl = bUrl.slice(0, -1) if (bUrl | length) > 1 and bUrl.slice(-1) == '/' else bUrl %}
                {% set bUrl = '' if bUrl == '/' else bUrl %}
                {% set isActive = (bRaw == curFull) if (bRaw.indexOf('?') > -1) else (bUrl == curPath) %}

                {# `--wide` goes position:static so the multi-column panel can
                   anchor to the bar instead of to this item — see the note on
                   `.hy-hrow` in style.css. #}
                <div class="hy-nav-item {{ 'hy-nav-item--wide' if hasDrop and wide }}"
                     {% if hasDrop %}@mouseenter="show({{ loop.index }})" @mouseleave="hide()"{% endif %}>

                  <a href="{{ b.nav_url | default('#', true) }}"
                     class="hy-nav-link {{ 'is-active' if isActive }} {{ 'is-hot' if b.nav_highlight }}"
                     {% if hasDrop %}@focus="show({{ loop.index }})" :aria-expanded="open === {{ loop.index }} ? 'true' : 'false'"{% endif %}>
                    <span>{{ b.nav_label }}</span>
                    {% if b.nav_badge %}<span class="hy-nav-badge">{{ b.nav_badge }}</span>{% endif %}
                    {% if hasDrop %}{{ caret('hy-caret hy-nav-caret') }}{% endif %}
                  </a>

                  {% if hasDrop %}
                    <div class="hy-drop {{ 'hy-drop--wide' if wide }}"
                         x-show="open === {{ loop.index }}"
                         x-cloak
                         @mouseenter="show({{ loop.index }})"
                         @mouseleave="hide()"
                         x-transition:enter="transition ease-out duration-200"
                         x-transition:enter-start="opacity-0 -translate-y-2"
                         x-transition:enter-end="opacity-100 translate-y-0"
                         x-transition:leave="transition ease-in duration-150"
                         x-transition:leave-start="opacity-100"
                         x-transition:leave-end="opacity-0">
                      <div class="hy-drop-inner">
                        <div class="hy-drop-links" style="--hy-drop-cols: {{ cols }};">
                          {{ menuLinks(b.nav_menu, 'hy-drop-link') }}
                        </div>

                        {% if promo and wide %}
                          <a href="{{ b.nav_image_url | default(b.nav_url, true) | default('#', true) }}" class="hy-drop-promo">
                            <img src="{{ promo }}" alt="{{ b.nav_image_caption | default('', true) }}" loading="lazy"/>
                            {% if b.nav_image_caption %}
                              <span class="hy-drop-promo-cap">{{ b.nav_image_caption }}</span>
                            {% endif %}
                          </a>
                        {% endif %}
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  {% endif %}
                </div>
              {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}

            {# ---- extra links, and the overflow that catches them ----
               The four nav BLOCKS are what the row is drawn for and they always
               stay: each can carry a mega-menu, and a mega-menu inside a
               dropdown is not a thing. `nav_extra_menu` items are plain links,
               so they are the ones that fold.

               Every extra link is printed TWICE — once as a row item and once
               as a `.hy-drop-link` in the panel — and the script below hides
               one copy or the other. Moving the node instead would mean
               rewriting its markup on every resize, because the row wants
               `.hy-nav-item > .hy-nav-link` and the panel wants a bare
               `.hy-drop-link`. Two copies and an `hidden` attribute is cheaper
               and cannot get the two out of step.

               ⚠️  Both lists are printed in the SAME order and the script pairs
               them by index. Anything added to one has to be added to the
               other. #}
            {% if navExtra %}
              {% set extraItems = (navExtra.items if navExtra.items else navExtra) %}

              {% for item in extraItems %}
                <div class="hy-nav-item" data-hy-nav-extra>
                  <a href="{{ item.url | default('#', true) }}"{{ extAttrs(item.url) }} class="hy-nav-link">
                    <span>{{ item.title }}</span>
                  </a>
                </div>
              {% endfor %}

              {# `hidden` at rest: with room for every link this item never
                 appears, and a merchant who picked a two-item menu on a wide
                 screen sees exactly what they picked. The script is what
                 reveals it. #}
              <div class="hy-nav-item hy-nav-item--more" data-hy-nav-more hidden
                   @mouseenter="show('more')" @mouseleave="hide()">
                <a href="#" class="hy-nav-link"
                   @click.prevent="open === 'more' ? close() : show('more')"
                   @focus="show('more')"
                   :aria-expanded="open === 'more' ? 'true' : 'false'">
                  <span>{{ t('header.more') }}</span>
                  {{ caret('hy-caret hy-nav-caret') }}
                </a>

                {# The same panel every other nav dropdown uses, at one column.
                   `open` is keyed by loop.index for the blocks above, so a
                   STRING key here can never collide with one of them. #}
                <div class="hy-drop hy-drop--more"
                     x-show="open === 'more'"
                     x-cloak
                     @mouseenter="show('more')"
                     @mouseleave="hide()"
                     x-transition:enter="transition ease-out duration-200"
                     x-transition:enter-start="opacity-0 -translate-y-2"
                     x-transition:enter-end="opacity-100 translate-y-0"
                     x-transition:leave="transition ease-in duration-150"
                     x-transition:leave-start="opacity-100"
                     x-transition:leave-end="opacity-0">
                  <div class="hy-drop-inner">
                    <div class="hy-drop-links" style="--hy-drop-cols: 1;">
                      {% for item in extraItems %}
                        <a href="{{ item.url | default('#', true) }}"{{ extAttrs(item.url) }}
                           class="hy-drop-link" data-hy-nav-folded hidden>{{ item.title }}</a>
                      {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            {% endif %}
          </nav>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      {# ---- centre: the brand ----
         Its own grid column, so it is centred on the bar and cannot drift when
         the nav or the action cluster changes width. #}
      <a href="/" class="hy-brand" aria-label="{{ storeName }}">
        {% if logo and logo.fileUrl %}
          {# Only the merchant's height rides inline. The width cap has to
             respond to the viewport and an inline style cannot, so the rest
             lives in style.css → "15.1 HEADER". #}
          <img src="{{ logo.fileUrl }}" alt="{{ storeName }}"
               class="hy-brand-logo" style="--hy-logo-h: {{ logoH }}px;"/>
        {% else %}
          <span class="hy-wordmark">{{ storeName }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      </a>

      {# ---- end: search prompt + icons ---- #}
      <div class="hy-hend">
        {% if showSearch %}
          {# ---- Search ----
             NOT a sheet. The reference expands the prompt INTO a 255×40 pill in
             the bar and hangs the results under it — the page stays where it is
             and the shopper keeps their place. The previous full-screen sheet
             (ui/search.njk, now removed) threw the whole page away to ask one
             question.

             The wrap is `position: relative` so the panel anchors to the field
             on desktop; below 1024 it goes static and the panel spans the bar —
             see "15.3 SEARCH" in style.css. #}
          <div class="hy-hsearch-wrap"
               x-data="hySearch({{ 'true' if (d.search_show_suggestions | default(true)) else 'false' }})"
               @click.outside="close()"
               @keydown.escape.window="close()">

            {# collapsed — the prompt #}
            <button type="button"
                    x-show="!open"
                    class="hy-hsearch {{ 'hy-hsearch--icon' if searchStyle == 'icon' }}"
                    @click="expand()"
                    aria-label="{{ t('header.search') }}">
              {% if searchStyle != 'icon' %}
                {# `, true` is load-bearing: Nunjucks' `default` fires on
                   UNDEFINED only, and this setting's schema default is "", which
                   is defined. Without it a merchant who never touched the field —
                   or who cleared it — gets an empty prompt and the translated
                   fallback never runs. #}
                <span class="hy-hsearch-text hy-desk">{{ d.search_placeholder | default(t('header.search_placeholder'), true) }}</span>
              {% endif %}
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/>
                <path stroke-linecap="round" d="m20 20-3.9-3.9"/>
              </svg>
            </button>

            {# expanded — a real form. `action` is set statically AND bound:
               Alpine boots at the end of <body>, so a bind-only action would
               submit to the current URL for anyone who hits Enter before then. #}
            <form class="hy-hfield"
                  x-show="open"
                  x-cloak
                  role="search"
                  method="get"
                  action="/shop"
                  @submit="open = false">
              <input type="search"
                     name="q"
                     x-ref="field"
                     x-model="q"
                     class="hy-hfield-input"
                     autocomplete="off"
                     @input.debounce.250ms="run()"
                     @keydown.arrow-down.prevent="move(1)"
                     @keydown.arrow-up.prevent="move(-1)"
                     @keydown.enter="if (enter()) $event.preventDefault()"
                     :aria-activedescendant="active >= 0 ? 'hy-sr-{{ id }}-' + active : null"
                     aria-autocomplete="list"
                     placeholder="{{ d.search_placeholder | default(t('header.search_placeholder'), true) }}"
                     aria-label="{{ t('header.search') }}"/>

              <button type="button"
                      class="hy-hfield-clear"
                      x-show="q.length > 0"
                      @click="clearQuery()">{{ t('pages.search.clear') }}</button>

              {# One slot, two jobs: submit while the panel is shut, close it
                 while it is open. Two buttons side by side would have put a ✕
                 next to a ⌕ that do nearly the same thing. #}
              <button type="submit"
                      class="hy-hfield-go"
                      x-show="!panelOpen"
                      aria-label="{{ t('header.search') }}">
                <svg width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" aria-hidden="true">
                  <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/>
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" d="m20 20-3.9-3.9"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
              <button type="button"
                      class="hy-hfield-go"
                      x-show="panelOpen"
                      x-cloak
                      @click="close()"
                      aria-label="{{ t('common.close') }}">
                <svg width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M6 18 18 6M6 6l12 12"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </form>

            {# ---- results panel ---- #}
            <div class="hy-spanel"
                 x-show="panelOpen"
                 x-cloak
                 x-transition:enter="transition ease-out duration-200"
                 x-transition:enter-start="opacity-0 -translate-y-2"
                 x-transition:enter-end="opacity-100 translate-y-0"
                 x-transition:leave="transition ease-in duration-150"
                 x-transition:leave-start="opacity-100"
                 x-transition:leave-end="opacity-0">

              <div x-show="loading" class="hy-spanel-state">
                <span class="hy-spinner" style="width: 22px; height: 22px;"></span>
              </div>

              <template x-if="!loading && (terms.length || results.length)">
                <div>
                  <template x-if="terms.length">
                    <div class="hy-spanel-block">
                      <p class="hy-spanel-head">{{ t('pages.search.suggestions') }}</p>
                      <div class="hy-spanel-chips">
                        <template x-for="term in terms" :key="term">
                          <a class="hy-chip" :href="'/shop?q=' + encodeURIComponent(term)" x-text="term"></a>
                        </template>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </template>

                  <template x-if="results.length">
                    <div class="hy-spanel-block">
                      <p class="hy-spanel-head">{{ t('pages.search.related') }}</p>
                      <div class="hy-sres">
                        <template x-for="(p, i) in results" :key="p._id">
                          <a class="hy-sres-card"
                             :id="'hy-sr-{{ id }}-' + i"
                             :class="active === i && 'is-active'"
                             @mouseenter="active = i"
                             :href="productUrl(p)">
                            <span class="hy-sres-media">
                              <template x-if="p.images && p.images.length">
                                <img :src="p.images[0].fileUrl" :alt="p.title" loading="lazy"/>
                              </template>
                              <template x-if="onSale(p)">
                                <span class="hy-sres-badge">{{ t('common.on_sale') }}</span>
                              </template>
                            </span>
                            <span class="hy-sres-name" x-text="p.title"></span>
                            <span class="hy-sres-money">
                              <span class="hy-sres-price" x-text="money(p.pricing && p.pricing.price)"></span>
                              <template x-if="onSale(p)">
                                <span class="hy-sres-was" x-text="money(p.pricing.compareAtPrice)"></span>
                              </template>
                            </span>
                          </a>
                        </template>
                      </div>

                      <a class="hy-btn hy-btn--solid hy-btn--pill hy-spanel-all" :href="allUrl()">
                        {{ t('pages.search.view_all') }}
                      </a>
                    </div>
                  </template>
                </div>
              </template>

              <div x-show="!loading && searched && !terms.length && !results.length" class="hy-spanel-state">
                <p>{{ t('pages.search.no_results') }}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        {% endif %}

        {% if actionUrl %}
          <a href="{{ actionUrl }}"{{ extAttrs(actionUrl) }}
             class="hy-icon-btn hy-desk"
             aria-label="{{ d.action_link_label | default(t('header.quick_link'), true) }}">
            {{ actionSvg(actionIcon) }}
          </a>
        {% endif %}

        {% if showCart %}
          <button type="button"
                  onclick="toggleModal('cart')"
                  class="hy-icon-btn hy-cart-btn"
                  aria-label="{{ t('header.cart') }}"
                  x-data>
            {# Drawn to fill the 24-box evenly rather than to a formula: the
               first pass hung the basket off the bottom-right and read as a
               different icon from the two beside it. #}
            <svg width="21" height="21" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                 stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M2.2 2.8h3l2.2 11a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.7 1.4h8.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.7-1.4l1.5-7.5H6.2"/>
              <circle cx="9.4" cy="20" r="1.4"/><circle cx="18" cy="20" r="1.4"/>
            </svg>
            {# The SSR count is PRINTED, and x-cloak is conditional.

               Alpine boots at the very end of <body>, and `x-text` writes
               nothing until it does — so an unconditionally cloaked, empty span
               left the badge missing for the first frames of EVERY page load,
               on a value the server already knew. On a slow connection a
               shopper with items in their cart sees an empty bag icon, which is
               the one thing this badge exists to prevent.

               With a count the span carries the number and no cloak, so it is
               painted with the page and Alpine takes over on the same value —
               no flash, nothing to reconcile. With no count the cloak hides it
               until `x-show` takes the same decision a moment later. #}
            {% set ssrQty = cart.totalQuantity | default(0, true) %}
            <span class="hy-count"
                  x-show="$store.cart.totalQuantity > 0"
                  x-text="$store.cart.totalQuantity"
                  {% if ssrQty == 0 %}x-cloak{% endif %}>{{ ssrQty }}</span>
          </button>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

</header>

{# ---- The search dimmer ----
   OUTSIDE <header>, and that is the whole point. The header is
   `position: fixed` with a z-index, which makes it a STACKING CONTEXT: a child
   of it can never paint below it, whatever z-index it is given. Rendered
   inside, this element dimmed the bar it belongs to — the one part of the page
   that has to stay lit while someone is typing in it.

   Out here it sits between the page and the header on the normal scale. #}
{% if showSearch %}
  <div class="taqa-overlay hy-sdim"
       x-data
       x-show="$store.search.open"
       x-cloak
       @click="$store.search.dismiss()"
       x-transition:enter="transition ease-out duration-200"
       x-transition:enter-start="opacity-0"
       x-transition:enter-end="opacity-100"
       x-transition:leave="transition ease-in duration-150"
       x-transition:leave-start="opacity-100"
       x-transition:leave-end="opacity-0"></div>
{% endif %}

{# Spacer — a fixed header no longer occupies flow space, so this reserves it.
   Its height is written by sync() below, which remeasures on every event that
   can change it. #}
{% if isSticky %}
  <div id="hy-header-spacer-{{ id }}" aria-hidden="true"></div>
{% endif %}

<script>
  (function () {
    var header = document.getElementById('hy-header-{{ id }}');
    if (!header) return;

    {% if isSticky %}
    var spacer = document.getElementById('hy-header-spacer-{{ id }}');

    /* Remeasured on every event that can change the header's height: a web font
       swapping in, a viewport resize, the announcement bar being dismissed.
       Setting it once on parse would leave a gap or an overlap the moment any
       of those fire.

       The measurement is taken in the FLOATING state, which is the taller
       one — it carries the top gap. Reserving the floating height and not the
       spread height is deliberate: the spacer only matters while the page is at
       the top, and the moment it is not, the bar is spread and shorter by
       exactly `float_gap`, which is scrolled past anyway. */
    var sync = function () {
      var h = header.offsetHeight;
      if (spacer) spacer.style.height = h + 'px';
      /* Same measurement, second consumer: html { scroll-padding-top } needs it
         so an #anchor clears the fixed header instead of landing behind it.
         Written on <html> because that is the element the property applies to. */
      document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--hy-header-h', h + 'px');
      var top = header.querySelector('.hy-topbar');
      header.style.setProperty('--hy-topbar-h', (top ? top.offsetHeight : 0) + 'px');
    };
    sync();
    window.addEventListener('load', sync);
    window.addEventListener('resize', sync);
    if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(sync);
    if (window.ResizeObserver) new ResizeObserver(sync).observe(header);
    {% endif %}

    /* ---- Announcement bar · dismiss ----
       sessionStorage, not localStorage: an announcement is a campaign, and a
       shopper who closes it should see the NEXT one. localStorage would keep it
       shut across visits and the merchant would never know why their banner
       stopped working.

       The key carries a hash of the message, so changing the text brings the
       bar back for everyone who dismissed the previous one. Without that, a
       merchant editing the announcement would be shouting at a closed room.

       Read and applied HERE, inline, while the body is still parsing: the bar
       is a few nodes above this script, so it is hidden before the browser has
       painted it and there is no flash of a bar that then vanishes.

       try/catch on every access — Safari private mode throws on the first read
       of sessionStorage, and an uncaught throw here would take the whole header
       script down with it. */
    (function () {
      var bar = document.getElementById('hy-topbar-{{ id }}');
      if (!bar) return;

      /* djb2 over the rendered message — short, stable, and enough to tell one
         announcement from the next. */
      var msg = {{ topMsg | default('', true) | dump | safe }};
      var h = 5381;
      for (var i = 0; i < msg.length; i++) h = ((h << 5) + h + msg.charCodeAt(i)) | 0;
      var KEY = 'hy-topbar-closed:' + (h >>> 0).toString(36);

      var closed = false;
      try { closed = sessionStorage.getItem(KEY) === '1'; } catch (e) {}
      if (closed) { bar.remove(); return; }

      var btn = document.getElementById('hy-topbarX-{{ id }}');
      if (!btn) return;
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        try { sessionStorage.setItem(KEY, '1'); } catch (e) {}

        /* Collapse, then remove. A bare remove() drops the bar's height out of
           the document in one frame and the whole page snaps upward — correct,
           and unpleasant enough to read as a glitch.

           The height has to be pinned to its measured pixel value first:
           `auto` is not an animatable value, so going straight to 0 from it
           transitions nothing. One forced reflow between the two writes is what
           makes the browser treat them as two states rather than collapsing
           them into the final one.

           `prefers-reduced-motion` skips to the end — this is a layout
           collapse, exactly the kind of motion that setting asks us not to
           make. */
        var reduce = document.documentElement.classList.contains('hy-no-motion') || (window.matchMedia
          && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches);
        if (reduce) { bar.remove(); return; }

        bar.style.height = bar.offsetHeight + 'px';
        bar.style.overflow = 'hidden';
        void bar.offsetHeight;                      /* forced reflow */
        bar.style.transition = 'height 240ms var(--ease-out), opacity 160ms linear';
        bar.style.height = '0px';
        bar.style.opacity = '0';

        /* transitionend can fail to arrive — a background tab throttles it, and
           a display change mid-flight swallows it — so the removal is on a
           timer that the event can only bring forward. */
        var done = false;
        var finish = function () { if (done) return; done = true; bar.remove(); };
        bar.addEventListener('transitionend', finish);
        setTimeout(finish, 320);
      });
    })();

    {% if navOn and navExtra %}
    /* ---- Nav overflow ----
       The row is a three-column grid whose outer columns are `minmax(0, 1fr)`,
       and that symmetry is the ONLY reason the brand sits dead centre. So the
       nav can never be wider than half the row minus the logo — measured at
       1024 the start cell is 431px and six Arabic labels come to 489. The
       `overflow: hidden` on `.hy-hstart` is what stops them painting over the
       brand, and what it does instead is cut the last one in half.

       So: the row shows what fits, and the rest goes in the panel. The blocks
       are never folded — only `nav_extra_menu` items, which is also the only
       list whose length the row was not drawn around.

       Measured against `scrollWidth`, not a sum of widths: the nav is a flex
       row inside an `overflow: hidden` cell, so its box is already clipped to
       the cell while `scrollWidth` still reports what the content wants. */
    var nav = header.querySelector('.hy-nav');
    var cell = header.querySelector('.hy-hstart');
    if (nav && cell) {
      var extras = [].slice.call(nav.querySelectorAll('[data-hy-nav-extra]'));
      var folded = [].slice.call(nav.querySelectorAll('[data-hy-nav-folded]'));
      var more   = nav.querySelector('[data-hy-nav-more]');

      var fitNav = function () {
        if (!more || !extras.length) return;

        /* Always measured from the everything-shown state. Folding from
           wherever the last pass left off cannot UNfold: once an item is
           hidden it stops counting toward scrollWidth, so a widening viewport
           would read "it fits" and never bring it back. */
        for (var i = 0; i < extras.length; i++) {
          extras[i].hidden = false;
          folded[i].hidden = true;
        }
        more.hidden = true;

        /* `.hy-desk` is display:none below 1024 — the burger owns the links
           there and the sidebar already lists every one of them. offsetParent
           is the cheapest way to ask whether this row is on screen at all. */
        if (!nav.offsetParent) return;
        if (nav.scrollWidth <= cell.clientWidth) return;

        /* Revealing "المزيد" costs width of its own, so it goes in BEFORE the
           loop counts — folding two links to make room for a third item that
           was not measured is how this kind of loop ends up one item short. */
        more.hidden = false;
        for (var j = extras.length - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
          extras[j].hidden = true;
          folded[j].hidden = false;
          if (nav.scrollWidth <= cell.clientWidth) break;
        }
      };

      fitNav();
      window.addEventListener('resize', fitNav);
      /* Cairo swaps in after first paint and every label changes width with it.
         Without this the fold is decided against the fallback face — which on
         Arabic is narrower, so it under-folds and the clipping comes back. */
      if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fitNav);
      window.addEventListener('load', fitNav);
    }
    {% endif %}

    {% if showSearch %}
    /* ---- Search ----
       Registered on `alpine:init` like every other component in this theme —
       defining it at parse time would race Alpine's boot at the end of <body>.

       `$store.search` exists only so the dimmer, which is a SIBLING of the
       field rather than a descendant, can see whether the panel is up. Alpine
       scopes x-data to its own subtree, so the two cannot share state any other
       way without wrapping half the header in a component. */
    document.addEventListener('alpine:init', function () {
      if (window.__hySearchReady) return;   /* one header per page, but the
                                               Theme Editor can re-inject it */
      window.__hySearchReady = true;

      /* `open` is REPORTED by the field (the dimmer reads it). `nonce` is the
         other direction — the dimmer bumps it to say "the user dismissed this",
         and the field watches it.

         They have to be two things. With one shared boolean, the field could
         not tell "the panel closed because the query got too short" from "the
         user clicked away", and treated both as the second: deleting down to
         one character shut the whole field, so the last letter could not be
         erased without reopening it. */
      Alpine.store('search', {
        open: false,
        nonce: 0,
        dismiss: function () { this.nonce++; }
      });

      Alpine.data('hySearch', function (showTerms) {
        /* `live` and `count` were two Theme Editor knobs and are literals now.
           Live suggestions are the whole point of an in-bar field — one that
           only answers on Enter may as well be the full-screen sheet this
           replaced — and the panel is drawn for THREE rows: a fourth runs it
           past the bottom of the bar on a laptop. */
        var COUNT = 3;
        return {
          q: '',
          open: false,
          loading: false,
          searched: false,
          results: [],
          terms: [],
          /* -1 = nothing highlighted, which is also "Enter submits the form and
             goes to the full results page". Any other value is an index into
             `results`, and Enter opens that product instead. */
          active: -1,

          /* The panel is derived, never assigned. Two booleans for "the field is
             open" and "the panel is up" drifted apart the moment anything closed
             one without the other — the dimmer stayed lit over a shut field. */
          get panelOpen() {
            return this.open && this.q.trim().length >= 2 &&
                   (this.loading || this.searched);
          },

          init: function () {
            /* The dimmer lives outside this component's tree, so the store is
               how it finds out. `$watch` rather than a setter on every path
               that can change the panel — there are five of them. */
            this.$watch('panelOpen', (v) => { Alpine.store('search').open = v; });
            /* A counter, not the boolean above: see the note on the store. This
               only ever fires when someone actually clicks the dimmer. */
            this.$watch('$store.search.nonce', () => this.close());
          },

          expand: function () {
            this.open = true;
            /* Focusing while the field is still display:none silently does
               nothing in every browser — wait for the paint. */
            this.$nextTick(() => this.$refs.field && this.$refs.field.focus());
          },

          close: function () {
            this.open = false;
            this.active = -1;
            Alpine.store('search').open = false;
          },

          clearQuery: function () {
            this.q = '';
            this.results = [];
            this.terms = [];
            this.searched = false;
            this.active = -1;
            this.$refs.field && this.$refs.field.focus();
          },

          /* Wraps at both ends: Down from the last lands back on the field
             (active = -1) rather than sticking, which is how a shopper gets back
             to editing what they typed without reaching for the mouse. */
          move: function (step) {
            if (!this.panelOpen || !this.results.length) return;
            var n = this.results.length;
            this.active = this.active + step;
            if (this.active >= n) this.active = -1;
            if (this.active < -1) this.active = n - 1;
          },

          /* Returns TRUE when it handled the key, so the caller knows whether to
             let the form submit. Enter on a highlighted row must not do both. */
          enter: function () {
            if (!this.panelOpen || this.active < 0 || !this.results[this.active]) return false;
            window.location.href = this.productUrl(this.results[this.active]);
            return true;
          },

          productUrl: function (p) { return '/products/' + (p.slug || p.handle || p._id); },
          allUrl: function () { return '/shop?q=' + encodeURIComponent(this.q.trim()); },
          money: function (v) { return Qumra.utils.formatMoney(v || 0); },
          onSale: function (p) {
            var c = p.pricing && p.pricing.compareAtPrice, x = p.pricing && p.pricing.price;
            return !!(c && c > x);
          },

          run: function () {
            var self = this;
            var q = (this.q || '').trim();
            /* A new query invalidates the highlight — index 2 of the old list is
               a different product in the new one. */
            this.active = -1;
            if (q.length < 2) { this.results = []; this.terms = []; this.searched = false; return; }

            this.loading = true;
            /* suggest() is ALREADY debounced 300ms inside main.js and its third
               argument is a RESULT LIMIT, not a delay. The @input debounce here
               is 250ms and they stack — which is the point: the outer one stops
               the spinner flashing on every keystroke, the inner one stops the
               request. */
            Qumra.search.suggest(q, function (data) {
              var r = (data && data.resources) || {};
              var list = r.products || (data && data.products) || [];
              self.results = list.slice(0, COUNT);
              /* Qumra returns `queries` on some stores and only `collections` on
                 others. Either is a reasonable chip; a collection is arguably the
                 better one, since it always leads somewhere that exists. */
              var terms = r.queries || [];
              if (!terms.length && r.collections)
                terms = r.collections.map(function (c) { return c.title; });
              self.terms = showTerms ? terms.slice(0, 6) : [];
              self.searched = true;
              self.loading = false;
            }, COUNT);
          }
        };
      });
    });
    {% endif %}

    {% if isFloat %}
    /* ---- The shape change ----
       `is-float` is ON at rest and comes OFF the moment the page moves; every
       animated property lives on that one class in the CSS.

       The threshold is 4px, not 0. A trackpad and an iOS rubber-band both emit
       scroll events at scrollY between 0 and 1 while the page has not actually
       moved, and a 0 threshold made the bar flicker between its two shapes
       under a resting finger.

       rAF-gated: `scroll` fires far more often than the screen repaints, and
       toggling a class that animates four properties on every one of those was
       measurably more work than the animation itself. */
    var ticking = false;
    var apply = function () {
      ticking = false;
      header.classList.toggle('is-float', window.scrollY <= 4);
    };
    apply();
    window.addEventListener('scroll', function () {
      if (ticking) return;
      ticking = true;
      window.requestAnimationFrame(apply);
    }, { passive: true });

    /* A reload restores the scroll position AFTER this script runs, and bfcache
       restores it with no scroll event at all — both leave a spread page
       wearing the floating bar. */
    window.addEventListener('load', apply);
    window.addEventListener('pageshow', apply);
    {% endif %}
  })();
</script>

{# ---- Global panels triggered from the header ---- #}
{% ui "sidebar.njk", nav_items=navItems, extra_menu=navExtra, currentLang=currentLang, showLang=showLocale, action_url=actionUrl, action_label=(d.action_link_label or "") %}
{#- Qalab's `ui` tag rejects an undefined argument and prints an error box
    instead of the drawer — every setting a merchant never touched (no upsell
    products, no empty-state collections) arrives undefined, so each one is
    given a defined fallback here. -#}
{% ui "cart.njk", free_shipping=(d.cart_free_shipping or 0), upsell_title=(d.cart_upsell_title or ''), upsell=(d.cart_upsell_products or []), empty_collections=(d.cart_empty_collections or []), footer_dark=(d.cart_footer_dark if d.cart_footer_dark is defined else true), note=(d.cart_note or '') %}

{# Shape and announcement colours. These are the widget's OWN style block and
   must stay ABOVE the section-colours include — both target the same id with
   identical specificity, so source order decides. #}
<style>
  /* The `-set` suffix is load-bearing. This block is an ID selector, so
     anything it writes beats every class rule in the stylesheet — including
     the responsive ones. Written to the plain names, the merchant's desktop
     gap and radius survived into a 390px viewport and the phone's own values
     in "15.1 RESPONSIVE" never applied.

     The stylesheet reads these as the DESKTOP values and decides what the
     narrower breakpoints use. */
  #hy-header-{{ id }} {
    --hy-float-w-set: {{ floatW }}px;
    --hy-float-gap-set: {{ floatGap }}px;
    --hy-float-r-set: {{ floatR }}px;
    --hy-topbar-bg: {{ d.topbar_bg | default('var(--color-accent)', true) }};
    --hy-topbar-fg: {{ d.topbar_text | default('var(--color-text-on-accent)', true) }};
  }
</style>

{# Per-section palette. Emits nothing unless `colors_enabled` is on, so the
   switch IS the revert. Must stay last — see the partial's header for why. #}
{% ui "section-colors.njk", scope='#hy-header-' ~ id, c=d %}
